{"ts": "2026-09-28 12:52:45", "level": "DEBUG", "event": "llm.context_sent", "status": "success", "chunks": [{"parent_id": "06f1604a-84d6-44ca-bec8-e380d36beabb", "text": "1. Warranty Information\nThe AquaFlow AF-200 is covered by a limited warranty period of 12 months from the date of purchase.\nThis warranty covers defects in materials and workmanship under normal use.\nThe warranty does not cover damage caused by improper installation, unauthorized repairs, or use with\nfluids other than clean fresh water. To make a warranty claim, contact AquaFlow customer support with\nyour original purchase receipt and the product serial number.\nExtended warranty coverage of up to 36 months is available for purchase separately within 90 days of\nthe original purchase date."}, {"parent_id": "731ab1ba-6d00-4e65-b1c9-984b662e8ddc", "text": "AquaFlow AF-200 Submersible Pump\nUser Manual & Technical Reference\nThis manual covers installation, operation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and warranty terms for the\nAquaFlow AF-200 submersible water pump."}, {"parent_id": "e7345438-1a19-48bb-afff-eaba19426dc6", "text": "5. Technical Specifications\n Specification\nValue\nModel\nAquaFlow AF-200\nMax flow rate\n200 liters per minute\nMax head height\n8 meters\nPower rating\n750 watts\nVoltage\n230V AC, 50Hz\nCable length\n10 meters\nMax water temperature\n35 degrees Celsius\nHousing material\nStainless steel and reinforced polymer\nWeight\n6.2 kg"}, {"parent_id": "f1aad0b2-f325-4bc0-addb-081f7421d59a", "text": "2. Installation Instructions\n2.1 Site Preparation\nSelect a mounting location with a firm, level base. The pump must be fully submerged in water at all\ntimes during operation. Never run the pump dry, as this will damage the internal seals within seconds.\n2.2 Electrical Connection\nThe AF-200 requires a dedicated 230V AC, 50Hz power supply protected by a residual current device\n(RCD) rated at 30mA or less. Do not connect the pump to an extension cord rated below 10 amps.\n2.3 Priming and First Start\nLower the pump slowly into the water, allowing air to escape from the intake housing. Once fully\nsubmerged, connect the power supply. The pump will begin operating automatically when the\nintegrated float switch rises above the low-water cutoff level."}], "request_id": "f2741914", "session_id": "46123eeefca7"}
