{"ts": "2026-09-28 12:57:10", "level": "INFO", "event": "chat.qa", "question": "both", "answer": "**AquaFlow AF‑200 (submersible pump)**  \n- Make sure the pump is **fully submerged** in water at all times; running it dry will damage the internal seals.  \n- Verify the **power connection**: the unit needs a dedicated 230 V AC, 50 Hz supply protected by an RCD ≤ 30 mA; check that the plug and cable are not worn or damaged.  \n- Inspect the **intake screen** weekly for debris and clean it if blocked.  \n- Every 6 months, remove the pump and **inspect the impeller** for wear.  \n- Annually replace the shaft seal (even if it looks fine).  \n- If the pump still does not operate after these checks, refer to the warranty section (12 months limited, extendable to 36 months) and contact AquaFlow customer‑service with your receipt and serial number.\n\n**AquaFlow AF‑300 (countertop beverage brewer)**  \n- If brewing stops, **verify that the reservoir is seated correctly** and contains sufficient water.  \n- If the unit does **not heat**, disconnect power and contact an authorized service provider.  \n- Perform routine maintenance: rinse the reusable stainless‑steel filter after each use and descale when mineral buildup is visible or brewing performance declines.  \n- The AF‑300 carries a **24‑month limited warranty** for manufacturing defects; keep your proof of purchase for any warranty claim.  \n\nAll steps are drawn directly from the supplied manuals; no external information is added. If the problem persists after following these checks, consult the warranty and contact the respective manufacturer’s support.", "sources": 8, "duration_ms": 41215, "budget": {"max_agent_iterations": 3, "max_llm_calls": 3, "max_retrieval_operations": 2, "max_guardrail_retries": 1, "agent_iterations": 1, "llm_calls": 3, "retrieval_operations": 1, "guardrail_retries": 0}, "request_id": "937d037d", "session_id": "46123eeefca7"}
