{"ts": "2026-09-28 12:57:31", "level": "DEBUG", "event": "llm.context_sent", "status": "success", "chunks": [{"parent_id": "6ed8fb57-ba69-4a27-9274-784def169982", "text": "SkyBrew Coffee Maker\nModel SB-450 — User Manual\n1. Introduction\nThank you for purchasing the SkyBrew SB-450 automatic coffee maker. This manual explains how to\nset up, operate, and maintain your device safely. Please read all instructions carefully before first use.\nThe SB-450 supports drip brewing, a programmable timer, and a built-in grinder for whole bean coffee.\n2. Safety Precautions\nDo not immerse the power cord, plug, or base unit in water or any other liquid. Always unplug the unit\nbefore cleaning or when not in use for an extended period. Keep the appliance out of reach of children.\nDo not operate the coffee maker if the power cord or plug is damaged, or after the appliance\nmalfunctions."}, {"parent_id": "fc3feded-a49f-4055-9d06-000b6e803018", "text": "5. Warranty Information\nSkyBrew warrants this product against defects in materials and workmanship for a period of 24 months\nfrom the date of purchase. This warranty covers manufacturing defects only. Coverage does not extend\nto damage caused by unauthorized repairs, misuse, or normal wear and tear such as descaling\ndeposits. To make a warranty claim, contact SkyBrew customer support with your proof of purchase.\n6. Troubleshooting\n6.1 Coffee Maker Will Not Turn On\nCheck that the unit is plugged into a working outlet. Ensure the power switch on the base is set to ON.\nIf the unit still does not power on, contact customer support.\n6.2 Coffee Tastes Weak or Bitter\nWeak coffee is often caused by using too little coffee or grounds that are too coarse. Bitter coffee can\nresult from over-extraction; try a coarser grind setting or reduce brew strength using the STRENGTH\ndial on the control panel.\n6.3 Descaling\nDescale the SB-450 every 60 brew cycles using a 1:3 mixture of white vinegar and water, or a\ncommercial descaling solution. Run one full brew cycle with the solution, followed by two full cycles of\nplain water to rinse."}, {"parent_id": "72f25ef1-5c6a-43e4-819c-b0a7f7c0130a", "text": "3. Setup Instructions\nRemove all packaging material and stickers from the coffee maker. Rinse the removable water\nreservoir and carafe with warm water before first use. Place the unit on a flat, dry, heat-resistant\nsurface at least 6 inches away from the wall.\n3.1 Filling the Water Reservoir\nOpen the reservoir lid on the back of the unit. Fill with fresh, cold water up to the desired line, not\nexceeding the MAX marking of 12 cups. Close the lid firmly before brewing.\n3.2 Loading Coffee Beans or Grounds\nFor whole beans, open the bean hopper and add up to 90 grams of beans. For pre-ground coffee,\nremove the hopper insert and add 1 tablespoon of grounds per cup directly into the filter basket."}], "request_id": "7f5481be", "session_id": "46123eeefca7"}
