{"ts": "2026-09-28 12:57:38", "level": "INFO", "event": "chat.qa", "question": "what about skybrew?", "answer": "**SkyBrew Coffee Maker (model SB‑450) – What to do if it isn’t working**\n\n- **Warranty** – The unit is covered by a 24‑month limited warranty for manufacturing defects only. To make a claim, contact SkyBrew customer support with your proof of purchase.  \n\n- **Troubleshooting (from the manual)**  \n  1. **Coffee maker will not turn on**  \n     - Verify that the plug is firmly inserted into a working outlet.  \n     - Ensure the power switch on the base is set to **ON**.  \n     - If it still does not power on, contact customer support.  \n\n  2. **Coffee tastes weak or bitter**  \n     - *Weak coffee*: Use more coffee or a finer grind.  \n     - *Bitter coffee*: Reduce brew strength via the **STRENGTH** dial, use a coarser grind, or decrease the amount of coffee.  \n\n  3. **Descaling** (to prevent performance issues)  \n     - Descale every **60 brew cycles**.  \n     - Use a 1:3 mixture of white vinegar and water **or** a commercial descaling solution.  \n     - Run one full brew cycle with the solution, then run two full cycles of plain water to rinse.  \n\nThese steps are taken directly from the SkyBrew SB‑450 user manual (warranty information and troubleshooting section). If the problem persists after following the above checks, refer to the warranty and contact SkyBrew customer support.", "sources": 3, "duration_ms": 13587, "budget": {"max_agent_iterations": 3, "max_llm_calls": 3, "max_retrieval_operations": 2, "max_guardrail_retries": 1, "agent_iterations": 1, "llm_calls": 3, "retrieval_operations": 1, "guardrail_retries": 0}, "request_id": "7f5481be", "session_id": "46123eeefca7"}
