{"ts": "2026-09-28 13:03:40", "level": "DEBUG", "event": "llm.context_sent", "status": "success", "chunks": [{"parent_id": "4f9ba188-406c-4037-b60f-c26e0027f297", "text": "Employee Handbook — Leave and Remote Work\nPolicy\n1. Purpose\nThis policy outlines the leave entitlements, remote work eligibility, and reporting procedures applicable\nto all full-time employees of the company, effective from the date of hire.\n2. Annual Leave\nEmployees accrue 18 days of paid annual leave per calendar year, credited monthly at a rate of 1.5\ndays. Unused leave up to 5 days may be carried over into the following year with manager approval.\nLeave requests must be submitted at least 5 working days in advance via the HR portal.\n3. Sick Leave\nEmployees are entitled to 10 days of paid sick leave per year. A medical certificate is required for\nabsences exceeding 2 consecutive days. Sick leave does not carry over and resets each calendar\nyear.\n4. Remote Work Eligibility\nEmployees who have completed their probation period (90 days) may apply for remote work\narrangements. Approval is subject to role suitability and manager discretion. Remote employees must\nremain reachable during core hours (10:00-16:00 local time) and attend in-person meetings when\nrequested with at least 3 days' notice.\n5. Reporting a Grievance\nEmployees who wish to raise a workplace grievance should first discuss the matter informally with their\ndirect manager. If unresolved, a formal written complaint may be submitted to Human Resources, who\nwill acknowledge receipt within 3 working days and aim to resolve the matter within 20 working days.\n6. Termination and Notice Periods\nEmployees who wish to resign must provide written notice of at least 30 days. The company reserves\nthe right to terminate employment for cause without notice, or without cause subject to statutory notice\nperiods and applicable severance pay."}], "request_id": "1a22129a", "session_id": "46123eeefca7"}
