{"ts": "2026-09-28 13:34:47", "level": "DEBUG", "event": "llm.context_sent", "status": "success", "chunks": [{"parent_id": "d7b66ed9-12f8-4368-aae1-faa3946df9e8", "text": "Patient Admission and Discharge Procedures\n1. Admission Process\nAll patients must be registered at the front desk prior to admission. Required documents include a valid\nphoto ID, insurance card (if applicable), and a referral letter for specialist departments. Emergency\nadmissions bypass standard registration and are processed directly through the Emergency\nDepartment triage desk.\n2. Ward Allocation\nPatients are allocated to wards based on the attending physician's assessment and bed availability.\nGeneral ward stays are billed per night; private and semi-private rooms carry an additional daily\nsurcharge as per the current rate card published by Billing.\n3. Visiting Hours\nStandard visiting hours are 11:00-13:00 and 17:00-19:00 daily. Intensive Care Unit visiting is restricted\nto immediate family, two visitors at a time, for 15 minutes per visit. Visiting hours may be suspended\nduring infection control precautions.\n4. Discharge Procedure\nDischarge is authorized by the attending physician once clinical criteria are met. Patients receive a\ndischarge summary, a medication list, and follow-up appointment details. Outstanding balances must\nbe settled at the Billing counter prior to leaving the premises, though this may be deferred in emergency\ncases.\n5. Medication and Follow-Up\nDischarged patients are provided a 7-day supply of prescribed medication where applicable. Follow-up\nappointments are scheduled within 14 days of discharge for surgical patients and within 30 days for\ngeneral medical admissions.\n6. Patient Rights and Complaints\nPatients have the right to access their medical records, request a second opinion, and lodge complaints\nregarding care quality through the Patient Relations office. Complaints are acknowledged within 48\nhours and investigated within 15 working days."}], "request_id": "4e6777ce", "session_id": "46123eeefca7"}
